; Expo SDK 54 pins react@19.1.0, but expo-router transitively depends on a
; react-dom whose peer is react@^19.2.6. npm 11 errors out on the mismatch
; with ERESOLVE. Expo Go / React Native doesn't use react-dom at runtime,
; so the legacy resolver is the safe way to install on a fresh clone.
legacy-peer-deps=true
